From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:31:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] podman: match equal database paths without resolving them

podman's database check resolves the symlinks of a recorded path and of
its own, the same string, in two calls, and resolves a path only if it
exists. Two podman commands starting together on a fresh /tmp/run then
fail now and then: one sees the run root that the other creates between
its two calls, and reports "database run root "/run/containers/storage"
does not match our run root "/tmp/run/containers/storage"".

Carry the podman patch that matches equal paths without resolving them.
It is meant for podman upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 utils/podman/Makefile                         |  2 +-
 ...atabase-paths-without-resolving-them.patch | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 utils/podman/patches/020-libpod-match-equal-database-paths-without-resolving-them.patch

diff --git a/utils/podman/Makefile b/utils/podman/Makefile
index cc75f88..0f5cc83 100644
--- a/utils/podman/Makefile
+++ b/utils/podman/Makefile
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=podman
 PKG_VERSION:=6.1.2
-PKG_RELEASE:=1
+PKG_RELEASE:=2
 
 PKG_SOURCE:=$(PKG_NAME)-$(PKG_VERSION).tar.gz
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/archive/v$(PKG_VERSION)
diff --git a/utils/podman/patches/020-libpod-match-equal-database-paths-without-resolving-them.patch b/utils/podman/patches/020-libpod-match-equal-database-paths-without-resolving-them.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3ad94bd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/utils/podman/patches/020-libpod-match-equal-database-paths-without-resolving-them.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] libpod: match equal database paths without resolving them
+
+ValidateDBConfig compares each path the database recorded with the
+runtime's own, after resolving the symlinks of each in turn. A path is
+resolved only if it exists, so when another process creates it between
+the two resolutions, the same path compares unequal:
+
+  database run root "/run/containers/storage" does not match our run
+  root "/tmp/run/containers/storage": database configuration mismatch
+
+It takes two podman processes starting at once, with a run root that
+goes through a symlink and does not exist yet: the storage creates the
+run root after the validation. That is how the first commands after a
+boot find it when /run is a symlink into a tmpfs. It is the same race as
+the volume path's (containers/podman#23515), for a path that the
+validation does not create.
+
+Resolve the paths only when they differ as strings: equal paths are the
+same path, however they resolve.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ libpod/sqlite_state.go | 4 +++-
+ 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/libpod/sqlite_state.go b/libpod/sqlite_state.go
+index 24fb7aa..609a715 100644
+--- a/libpod/sqlite_state.go
++++ b/libpod/sqlite_state.go
+@@ -408,7 +408,9 @@ func (s *SQLiteState) ValidateDBConfig(_ *Runtime) (defErr error) {
+ 	}
+ 
+ 	checkField := func(fieldName, dbVal, ourVal string, isPath bool) error {
+-		if isPath {
++		// Equal paths need no resolving: resolving the same path twice
++		// differs only when another process creates it in between.
++		if isPath && dbVal != ourVal {
+ 			// Tolerate symlinks when possible - most relevant for OStree systems
+ 			// and rootless containers, where we want to put containers in /home,
+ 			// which is symlinked to /var/home.
